  {
    "number": 149,
    "title": "Make guide status and next steps clear",
    "body": "Issue status was buried in long guide paragraphs. Every issue link now carries a status icon and label, and each guide leads with its outcome and next step. Closed delivery rows and evidence remain expandable. Selected parallel units are withheld when their saved labels or dependencies make them unavailable.\n\nRefs #148. The user requested both the repository guide and the public website. Public publication follows the verified source merge in a separate linked PR.\n\nValidation: guide generation, 8 Python maintenance tests and browser checks passed at 320, 390, 768, 900, 1000 and 1440 px. Checks cover visible and accessible status, keyboard links, evidence disclosure/search restoration, navigation, diagrams/viewers and actual PDF restoration; zero guide external requests or page errors. Rebuilding the committed output produces no drift. Before the fix, the completed-link regression failed because data-status was absent. Screenshots, PDF and the browser receipt are retained outside Git.\n\nThe refreshed snapshot covers 92 open issues in 12 guides, 131 referenced issues and 9 architecture viewers. The historical and architecture timestamps remain separate. Desktop-control defaults now match the owning issues. No product behavior/contracts changed, so no product OpenSpec change is needed. This is exempt guide UI under docs/sdlc.md; no human UI approval is required.\n\nReview comparison: base/merge-base `7c5957f7eed4bf8d52b6c68ae63c113c3788a834`, head `b68f3b7654139486f6d1d7aea664f04bc8964cdb`; `git diff BASE...HEAD`, clean worktree. Independent Standards and Specification reviews are underway against those commits.\n\nGuide-only CI evidence: both unchanged workflows, `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and `.github/workflows/work-guide.yml`, exclude `docs/work-guide/**` for pull_request and main push. The complete comparison below is entirely within that folder, with no renames or deletions. Current-head run/check/event and merge-state readbacks will be recorded before merge. The branch-protection endpoint returned HTTP 403 with the repository-plan limitation; no protection bypass is proposed.\n\nHTML SHA-256: `b4fdf012993abdfbd1f748f7ed2579ac2a3b3fb802aa2d0f87c4dcc569b47df8`.\n\nChanged paths:\n\n- `docs/work-guide/README.md`\n- `docs/work-guide/outputs/agent-device-work-guides.html`\n- `docs/work-guide/updates.md`\n- `docs/work-guide/work/backlogs/agent-device-hub-digest.txt`\n- `docs/work-guide/work/backlogs/agent-device-hub-issues.json`\n- `docs/work-guide/work/backlogs/agent-device-hub-prs.json`\n- `docs/work-guide/work/backlogs/divoom-app-upgrade-issues.json`\n- `docs/work-guide/work/backlogs/guide-coverage.json`\n- `docs/work-guide/work/backlogs/hub-native-deps.json`\n- `docs/work-guide/work/backlogs/snapshot.json`\n- `docs/work-guide/work/build_guide.py`\n- `docs/work-guide/work/check_guide.cjs`\n- `docs/work-guide/work/guide_paths.py`\n- `docs/work-guide/work/guide_reading.css`\n- `docs/work-guide/work/guide_status.py`\n- `docs/work-guide/work/test_maintenance.py`\n- `docs/work-guide/work/timeline.py`\n",
